node_modules
dist
build
*.tsbuildinfo
.turbo
.pytest_cache
__pycache__
*.pyc
.env
.env*.local
# Private-index pull-token dotenvs that tools/uv.sh reads (never commit a token).
.env.registry
.env.gemfury
.DS_Store
*.log
# Keyless GCP auth (google-github-actions/auth) drops a credentials file in the workspace during the
# e2e; ignore it so it doesn't make the tree dirty (the CLI vendors the COMMITTED branch, and the
# generate_app.py harness refuses to run on a dirty tree).
gha-creds-*.json
# Temp files written by `--check` runs of the descriptor and docs generators
# (build-registry.ts / build-docs-graph.ts) while diffing; removed on success, but
# a killed run would otherwise leave them and dirty the tree the e2e refuses.
.registry.expected.json
.README.expected.md

# Generated by .github/workflows/publish.yaml at publish time.
.npmrc

# NOTE: a capability template must NOT carry a literal `.npmrc` — the rule above drops it from the
# git subtree, and npm/bun strip it from every published tarball. The app-facing mapping therefore
# ships as `.npmrc.hbs`; the CLI removes the suffix after rendering the otherwise static file.

# Python virtualenvs (from the security-tooling side of the merge)
.venv/

# The Warden token action (mistralai/reusable-workflows/warden-token) runs
# `node ./tools/ci/warden-cli/cli.cjs` and skips its own dependency install when
# clipanion is already present. Vendoring the two runtime deps keeps that action
# working without a pnpm workspace, which cannot coexist with this bun monorepo
# root (pnpm always treats the root package.json as an importer, so `catalog:` /
# `workspace:*` specs break `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`).
!tools/ci/warden-cli/node_modules/
!tools/ci/warden-cli/node_modules/**
